class Solution {
public:
    int maximumUnits(vector<vector<int>>& boxTypes, int truckSize) {
        sort(boxTypes.begin(), boxTypes.end(),
             [](vector<int>& a, vector<int>& b) {
                 return a[1] > b[1];
             });

        int units = 0;

        for (auto box : boxTypes) {
            int boxes = min(truckSize, box[0]);
            units += boxes * box[1];
            truckSize -= boxes;

            if (truckSize == 0)
                break;
        }

        return units;
    }
};


Intuition: Pick boxes having the highest units first to maximize total units.
Algorithm: Sort box types by units per box in descending order.
Greedy: Take as many boxes as possible from the highest-unit type.
Time Complexity: O(n log n)
Space Complexity: O(1) extra space (excluding sorting space).
